|~ `::cell`, the kind of the identity under which a host keeps a value for
   the work with state, and what is declared under it: its invariant and
   its laws; its word `answer` is its host's.
   The rules it holds: [QSHST#cell]. ~|

:cell
  |~~ A cell is the interface a host gives for the work with state inside
      the language: an identity under its tag, `::cell"a3f9c2d1e04b"`,
      letters, digits and hyphens, whose literal reads back as itself in any
      later query, and its word `answer`, which its host declares and which
      reads at the call what the host keeps under it. A host of the streams
      keeps so an answer past the budget of every answer and a fact of a
      failure past the room of a fact, which the alert names instead of them,
      `:answer ::cell"…"`, under the identity of the query and what it keeps.
      So one value of one query is one cell, and
      `::cell"a3f9c2d1e04b" | answer | take 3` reads the first three
      elements of the whole. A host that keeps no cell names
      none, and its `answer` refuses a cell it does not hold.
      ::link~(::qlang/AnswerBeyondBudgetError) ::link~(::qlang/hosts)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ The identity of the cell, letters, digits and hyphens. ~~|
        ::string
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ A cell is named by its identity, a string,
            `::cell"a3f9c2d1e04b"`.
        ~~|
    | holds :PayloadNotIdentityError
        |~~ The identity of a cell is letters, digits and hyphens, so it
            names no folder past the store its host keeps.
        ~~|
        ~(contains #"^[A-Za-z0-9-]+$")
    | proves :readsBackAsItself
        |~~ A cell reads back as itself. ~~|
        ~(::cell"a3f9c2d1e04b" | eq (print | parse | answer))
    | proves :PayloadNotIdentityError/refusesASlash
        |~~ An identity that holds a slash is refused. ~~|
        ~(::cell"../notes" !| tag | eq ::cell/PayloadNotIdentityError)
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number names no cell. ~~|
        ~(::cell#12 !| tag | eq ::cell/PayloadKindNotTakenError);
